specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:12:- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L22), [validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:13:- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property with its field and expected type without leaking its value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L41), [validated by: names a wrong-typed property when the schema omits the root object type](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L64), [validated by: names the nested field path when a property has the wrong type](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L154), [validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:14:- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults ([validated by: passes valid input with undeclared properties through unchanged exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L130)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:15:- When `input` violates an `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a rejection naming the failing field and enum constraint without invoking the executor ([validated by: names the field and enum constraint when a property is not one of its allowed values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L173)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:16:- When a runtime payload is not an object, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a schema rejection instead of failing while recording input keys ([validated by: returns a schema rejection for a non-object runtime payload](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L193)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:21:- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at registration time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L4), [validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:22:- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: reuses a static schema validator across ten executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L80)).
